          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            A
            %strong bridge
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+diagram"} knot diagram
            is an arc that is the overpass in at least one crossing.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %strong bridge number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(K)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot"} knot
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the minimum number of bridges occurring in a diagram of the knot.
          %p
            By convention the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unknot"} unknot
            has bridge number equal to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            Almost by default this gives a knot invariant as it takes the minimum over all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+diagram"} knot diagrams
            that represent the isotopy class of the knot. (There is some work to do, but this is left for the moment!)
